|money drop = 1,080¢ - 4,266¢
}}

==Enemy==
Commander Ostromeda's stats are comparable to a 200% R.Ost, with 20k more health and 400 less attack power, while also having a slightly longer backswing and exchanging [[Critical Hit]]s for a 15% chance to warp units back by 800 range for 6.67 seconds. In spite of having the warp ability, Ostromeda's not a [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]], so only the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] are needed to keep their stats in check.

Commander Ostromeda is often buffed to 200%, giving them enough attack power (28k) to OHKO a level 50 [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]].

==Strategy==
This enemy might seem scary at first knowing how difficult other [[R.Ost]] variants can be, and it does pose a threat when buffed, but in reality, their [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] trait means they shouldn't be that hard to counter. You can stack [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] debuffers like [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] or [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Bakery Cat]] to impede them, and to further help with stalling [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] is also recommended, as it can tank Alien attacks and is Warp-immune. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] may struggle without aid from other units or by a lucky slip-in, as he's outranged by 20.

