==Trivia==
*Ostromeda is a portmanteau of ''ostrich'' and ''[[wikipedia:Andromeda|Andromeda]]'' (a well-known [[wikipedia:Andromeda (constellation)|constellation]] and the [[wikipedia:Andromeda (galaxy)|galaxy]] within it). It may also involve ''astromancy'', ''astrometry'', ''astrometria'' (Italian for astrometry), ''ostrom'' (Hungarian for siege), or the Polish female surname ''Ostromecka''.
*Commander Ostromeda's Japanese name, Androme Da-chōkan (アンドロメ・ダ長官, "Secretary Androme Da"), is derived from ''Andromeda'', 駝鳥 ''dachō'' (ostrich) and 長官 ''chōkan'' (secretary of government).
*The phrase 首を長くして待つ ''kubi o nagaku shite matsu'' in Commander Ostromeda's Japanese description is an idiom meaning "to eagerly wait", but literally translates to "to elongate one's neck and wait", which may be a joke about ostriches having long necks.
*Like [[R.Ost]] and most of his other variants, Commander Ostromeda appears to peck twice when they attack, yet doesn't have multi-hit, and as such only one peck does damage while the other is just backswing.
*Much like [[Super Metal Hippoe]], [[Angel Fanboy]] and many [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] and [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemies before them, [[Puffzerker]] and Commander Ostromeda were technically event enemies for a short time, until their proper introduction to [[Zero Legends]] in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]].
**Both Puffzerker and Commander Ostromeda debuted in the [[Anniversary/12 1/2 Year|12th and 1/2 Anniversary]], making them the only enemies from anniversary events to have descriptions.
**Since the 12th and 1/2 Anniversary still hadn't been released outside of Japan by the time [[Patisserie Parklands]] was added to other versions, Commander Ostromeda's first appearance in all versions except [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] was [[Creamy Snowplain]].
*Commander Ostromeda, [[Satan Claus]], [[Bears Be Back]] and [[Gorilliam]] are the only [[:Category:Unstarred Alien Enemies|unstarred Aliens]] with the Warp ability.
**Commander Ostromeda is the only one to have a description and the only one who was not introduced in a Lucky Ticket G event.

